      {
        "h_title": "Southern Hua Hin: Soi 67 and surrounds",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hua Hin",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "A 15-minute walk from the night market and train station but a one-minute hop to a decent stretch of beach, Soi 67 hosts a tightly packed selection of similarly equipped guesthouses in the 600 to 1,200 baht range. It also has a small, shabby swimming pool shared among the guesthouses. This general vicinity also includes a few upscale resorts, and a cluster of expat bars and guesthouses on Soi 80.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Bayan",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hua Hin",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Located smack on a quiet stretch of beach towards the south of Hua Hin, Baan Bayan is an elegant boutique resort centred on a gorgeous 90-year-old wooden house. Located inside the house, the priciest rooms are among the most romantic in Hua Hin. Each comes with high ceilings, cream-wooden walls, several swing-open windows, sumptuous wood floors, bright modern art and turquoise floral bed... Read our full review of Baan Bayan including room rates and direct contact details.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/southern_thailand/prachuap_khiri_khan/hua_hin/all/6586",
